Article 2 (Approval of Budget)
(1) Where the Korea Trade Insurance Corporation (hereinafter referred to as the "Corporation") intends to obtain approval of its budget pursuant to Article 55 of the Trade Insurance Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") and Article 19 of the Enforcement Decree of that Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Decree"), it shall submit the budget to the Minister of Trade and Industry, accompanied by the following documents: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jan. 21, 2022; Oct. 1, 2025>
1. A trade insurance business plan and a financial plan for the relevant year;
2. An estimated income statement and an estimated statement of financial position for the relevant year;
3. The income statement and statement of financial position for the preceding year, and their accompanying documents.
(2) Where the Corporation intends to amend a budget approved by the Minister of Trade and Industry, it shall submit to the Minister of Trade and Industry the documents referred to in paragraph (1) concerning the proposed amendment and obtain approval therefor. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Oct. 1, 2025>
